/// known-gap: interp stores a copy of the object in the field, so writes through the field never reach it
/// In a DES `every` block, a write through a field that holds an object
/// changes that object: two people eat from one village each tick.
<>Village |
    food: 10
xx
<>Person |
    home: nil
    every 1 tick
        self >> home >> food |= self >> home >> food - 1
    end
xx
v <> Village | food: 10
a <> Person | home: v
b <> Person | home: v
repeat 3
    tick()
end
say(v >> food)
